From 05956041db8fdcedba1510a0692d56029fbfb87f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "iLinux local research (AI-generated draft)" <local@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] dt-bindings: apple: Document t6050 (M5 Max) compatibles
 used by the draft DT

Add the t6050 compatibles referenced by the draft t6050/J716c device
tree so that dtbs_check can validate it:

  - board: apple,j716c + apple,t6050 (Mac17,6, MacBook Pro 16-inch M5 Max)
  - CPU cores: apple,sotra-m / apple,sotra-p (placeholder names following
    the M4 apple,donan-e/-p scheme; m1n1 calls the SoC family "Sotra" and
    the new core type "M core")
  - apple,t6050-pmgr, apple,t6050-pmgr-pwrstate (t8103 fallbacks)
  - apple,t6050-aic3 (t8122-aic3 fallback, 3 interrupt cells)
  - apple,t6050-pinctrl, apple,t6050-i2c, apple,t6050-wdt
  - apple,t6050-dart (t8110 fallback; ADT compatible "dart,t8110")
  - apple,t6050-asc-mailbox (asc-mailbox-v4 fallback; ADT IOPs are
    "iop,ascwrap-v6", m1n1 drives them with the v4 register layout)
  - apple,t6050-cluster-cpufreq (t8112 fallback, 5-bit p-state field)
  - apple,t6050-smc (t8103-smc fallback, as t6020/t8122; added 2026-10-16
    with the SMC node of the draft DT)

Evidence: ADT of a Mac17,6 (J716c), sanitized capture; m1n1 PR #610
(commit b2d3f5eba7ce) for the core naming.  The AIC of t6050 reports
aic-numdies-per-die = 2 in the ADT; whether 4-cell specifiers are needed
for second-die interrupts is unknown, so the 3-cell form is used.

Status: dt_binding_check DT_SCHEMA_FILES=apple reports nothing for the
files this series touches and dtbs_check of t6050-j716c.dtb reports 0
findings, dtschema 2026.9 (iLinux VM job 044, 2026-10-16).  The core
names stay placeholders.

NOT FOR UPSTREAM SUBMISSION: AI-generated local research draft (Asahi
Linux generative-AI policy).  No Signed-off-by on purpose.

